@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.Tracks.UI

@*
    Help content for the Tracks module.
*@

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud Tracks is a project management module for tracking work across products, epics, features, and
            work items. Use kanban boards, backlogs, sprints, and a range of planning views to organize and track your
            projects from start to finish.</p>
            <p>Work is organized in a hierarchy: <strong>Products</strong> contain <strong>Epics</strong>, epics contain
                <strong>Features</strong>, and features are broken into <strong>Items</strong>. Each level has its own
                kanban board.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="help-section">
                <h2 class="help-section-title">Products</h2>
                <p><strong>Creating a product:</strong> Click <strong>+ New Product</strong> on the product list and follow the
                    creation wizard. Products can be edited, soft-deleted, and restored.</p>
                    <p>Selecting a product opens its <strong>Kanban</strong> board, with additional views available from the
                        sidebar: <strong>List</strong>, <strong>Calendar</strong>, <strong>Dashboard</strong>,
                        <strong>Roadmap</strong>, <strong>Backlog</strong>, <strong>Timeline</strong>, <strong>Review</strong>, and
                        <strong>Settings</strong>.</p>
                    </section>

                    <section class="help-section">
                        <h2 class="help-section-title">Kanban Board</h2>
                        <p>The kanban board organizes work into swimlanes and columns. Create <strong>Epics</strong> (at product level),
                            <strong>Features</strong> (inside an epic), or <strong>Items</strong> (inside a feature) with the board's
                            add buttons, then drag cards between swimlanes to update their status in real time.</p>
                            <p>Open a card to edit its details — title, description, priority, story points, due date, and assignees.</p>
                        </section>

                        <section class="help-section">
                            <h2 class="help-section-title">Backlog</h2>
                            <p>The backlog lists work that hasn't been scheduled. Prioritize items by reordering them and move them into
                                sprints or onto the board when they're ready.</p>
                            </section>

                            <section class="help-section">
                                <h2 class="help-section-title">Sprints</h2>
                                <p>Plan time-boxed sprints with the <strong>Sprint Planning</strong> view and the <strong>Year Plan
                                    Wizard</strong>. Assign backlog items to sprints, track completion with burndown charts, and use the
                                    sprint panel to manage sprint scope per epic.</p>
                                </section>

                                <section class="help-section">
                                    <h2 class="help-section-title">Dashboard, Roadmap &amp; Timeline</h2>
                                    <p>The <strong>Dashboard</strong> shows product metrics and sprint velocity. The <strong>Roadmap</strong> lays
                                        out epics and features over time, the <strong>Timeline</strong> provides a year view, and the
                                        <strong>Calendar</strong> displays work by date.</p>
                                    </section>

                                    <section class="help-section">
                                        <h2 class="help-section-title">Review Sessions</h2>
                                        <p>Start a <strong>Live Review Session</strong> from the Review view to synchronize work-item navigation with
                                            your team and run planning poker in real time.</p>
                                        </section>

                                        <section class="help-section">
                                            <h2 class="help-section-title">Teams &amp; Saved Views</h2>
                                            <p>Manage <strong>Teams</strong> from the sidebar. Create <strong>Saved Views</strong> (custom views) to filter
                                                and display work items by your criteria for quick access from the sidebar.</p>
                                            </section>

                                            <section class="help-section">
                                                <h2 class="help-section-title">Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>
                                                <p>Press <kbd>?</kbd> to view all keyboard shortcuts, <kbd>/</kbd> to focus search, <kbd>←</kbd>/<kbd>→</kbd> to
                                                    navigate the epic/feature hierarchy, and <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> to submit a form. Use <strong>Show
                                                    Tour</strong> at the bottom of the sidebar for an in-app introduction.</p>
                                                </section>

                                                <section class="help-section">
                                                    <h2 class="help-section-title">Trash</h2>
                                                    <p>Soft-deleted work items are kept in the product's trash, where they can be restored.</p>
                                                </section>

                                                <section class="help-section">
                                                    <h2 class="help-section-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2>
                                                    <ul class="help-tips">
                                                        <li>Use the backlog to capture ideas before committing them to a sprint.</li>
                                                        <li>Saved views help you focus on specific priorities or team members.</li>
                                                        <li>Press <kbd>?</kbd> to discover keyboard shortcuts.</li>
                                                    </ul>
                                                </section>
                                            </div>
